OpenAI pure Yang–Mills construction: October submission and group verification

The original October submission is reproduced without changes in submission/.
Its NOTICE, LICENSE, THIRD_PARTY.md and third_party_licenses/ are retained there.

The verification package contains work from the Yang–Mills verification group,
including the previously developed Cherkis–Douglas–Jaffe–Nissim–Rajasekaran
problem formulation and the Douglas–Mei–Yin Osterwalder–Schrader specification.
The OS declarations and supporting formalizations derive from
xiyin137/OSreconstruction and math-commons/yang-mills. Selected lattice gauge
theory definitions derive from mrdouglasny/lgt. Existing source headers and
copyright notices have been preserved. Copies of the upstream Apache-2.0
licenses are in provenance/licenses/.

The Lean bridges in checks/ were assembled from the group's earlier review
work; their exact source commits and hashes are in provenance/review-imports.json.
Vendored and excerpted files may redirect imports, add namespace/section
wrappers or use a Lean-version compatibility setting. The changes and source
correspondences are recorded in provenance/ and evidence/historical/.
Original upstream snapshots in provenance/ are supplied for comparison, not
as additional compiled dependencies. scripts/verify.py and the release
documentation are new packaging and reproduction work, licensed Apache-2.0.

